{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[A]Well I gotta girl and you got none, Little Liza Jane
[A]My little gal she call me hun, [E]Little Liza [A]Jane
My little girl she’s sweet as pie, Little Liza Jane
She’s the apple of my eye, Little Liza Jane
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Oh sweet Liza, Little Liza Jane
Oh sweet Liza, Little Liza Jane  x2
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
My little girl lives in Baltimore, Little Liza Jane
Dog and children run round that door, Little Liza Jane
The stars are grey when she’s away, Little Liza Jane
And the sun never sets when she stays, Little Liza Jane
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
My little girl’s from New Orleans, Little Liza Jane
She’s the prettiest thing I’ve ever seen, Little Liza Jane
She drinks her liquor and has a ball, Little Liza Jane
And when we’re alone she gives me all, Little Liza Jane
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh all the girls there’s one I love, Little Liza Jane
When she’s at home there’s singing doves, Little Liza Jane
When the sun goes down & the moon comes out, Little Liza Jane
That’s when I begin to shout, Little Liza Jane
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus}
All her love she gives to me, Little Liza Jane
And all of mine she has from me, Little Liza Jane
Wedding bells they gonna ring, Little Liza Jane
Just the thought of her makes me sing, Little Liza Jane
{end_of_chorus}
